Two things in this project derive from licensecheck:

1. The license-identification algorithm. The modules under
   src/licenseclassifier/_engine/ are a Python port of licensecheck's Go
   sources — dictionary.py from internal/match/dict.go, resyntax.py from
   internal/match/resyntax.go, matcher.py from internal/match/rematch.go and
   internal/match/regexp.go, and scan.py from scan.go.

2. The built-in license patterns. The 423 patterns under data/licenses/ that are
   not marked as generated are the contents of licensecheck's licenses/ directory
   (the LRE pattern corpus), converted from Go template sources to plain LRE.
   src/licenseclassifier/_engine/licenses.json.gz is built from data/, and
   src/licenseclassifier/_engine/scanner.bin.gz is a compiled form of it.

   The remaining patterns were generated by this project from the SPDX matching
   templates (see below) and are not licensecheck's work.

